---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProductCard from '../../components/ProductCard.astro';
import { catalogProducts } from '../../lib/catalog';
import { trackedOutboundUrl } from '../../lib/outbound';

const qcProducts = catalogProducts.filter((product) => product.qcPhotoCount > 0).sort((a, b) => b.qcPhotoCount - a.qcPhotoCount).slice(0, 8);
const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Do QC photos prove an item is authentic or high quality?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No. QC photos show a particular item at a particular moment. They can help identify visible differences but do not independently verify authenticity, materials, durability or seller claims.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Why can QC photos look different from a listing?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Warehouse lighting, camera processing, screen settings and the selected variant can change how an item appears. Check the chosen option and overall construction first.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is a QC photo count a quality rating?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No. A QC count only indicates that warehouse reference images are associated with an indexed card. Review the actual images and make your own decision.' } }
  ]
});
---
<BaseLayout title="Oopbuy QC Photos: What to Check Before Shipping (2026) | OopbuyTop" description="Browse Oopbuy finds with warehouse QC photos, then use a practical QC checklist before shipping.">
  <section class="qc-finds qc-primary" id="qc-finds">
    <div class="section-heading qc-finds-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A1 · QC finds</p><h1>Finds that include<br />warehouse QC photos</h1></div><a class="button button-hot" href={trackedOutboundUrl('https://maisonlooks.com', 'qc_hero_cta')} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer">Browse live finds ↗</a></div>
    <p class="qc-intro">Cards show QC photo counts when available. Open a find to compare the live listing and warehouse reference images before you decide about shipping.</p>
    <div class="product-grid">{qcProducts.map((product) => <ProductCard product={product} placement="qc_card" />)}</div>
    <p class="qc-panel-note">Card images are product previews. Review the full warehouse QC set and current listing details before you approve a parcel.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="qc-workflow">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">B1 · Flow</p><h2>How QC fits the order process</h2></div>
    <ol>
      <li><b>01</b><div><strong>Choose a focused find</strong><span>Start with a product card, then open the current listing and selected option.</span></div></li>
      <li><b>02</b><div><strong>Review it at the warehouse</strong><span>Use QC photos to compare the received item with the order record.</span></div></li>
      <li><b>03</b><div><strong>Resolve a clear question</strong><span>Ask through the current agent workflow before the parcel is created.</span></div></li>
      <li><b>04</b><div><strong>Plan shipping separately</strong><span>Check destination, service and restrictions in live checkout information.</span></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="qc-focus-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">C1 · Checkpoints</p><h2>Check what matters for the item.</h2><p class="section-intro">QC is a comparison tool, not a quality score or authenticity test.</p></div></div>
    <div class="qc-focus-grid">
      <article><span>👟</span><h3>Shoes</h3><p>Compare the pair, size label, sole, shape, stitching and any hardware you care about.</p></article>
      <article><span>🧥</span><h3>Clothing</h3><p>Check size label, measurements, print placement, seams and the selected colour or fabric option.</p></article>
      <article><span>👜</span><h3>Bags & accessories</h3><p>Look at the shape, hardware, straps, interior label and included pieces where relevant.</p></article>
      <article><span>🎧</span><h3>Electronics</h3><p>Confirm the model, visible condition, included parts and compatibility details from the live listing.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="prose qc-article">
    <p class="eyebrow">D1 · Detailed QC guide</p>
    <h2>Use QC with the original listing</h2>
    <p>QC photos are warehouse reference photos taken after an item arrives. They can help you compare what reached the warehouse with the option you intended to buy before it is packed into an international parcel. They are useful evidence, but not a guarantee of product quality or future condition.</p>
    <p>Keep the original listing open while you review QC. Check the product title, variant, colour, size and quantity against your order record. Listings can be edited after purchase, so a saved screenshot or written note from the time you chose the item makes this comparison easier.</p>
    <h2>Start with the order details, not the photo count</h2>
    <ul><li>Does the visible item match the colour or material option selected?</li><li>Is the size label consistent with the size you ordered?</li><li>Are both items present when the order is a pair or set?</li><li>Are expected accessories, labels or packaging visible when those details matter?</li></ul>
    <p>This first pass prevents a common mistake: assessing workmanship before confirming that the warehouse received the correct version of the item.</p>
    <h2>How many QC photos are enough?</h2>
    <p>More photos can provide more angles, but a high number is not a quality score. Four clear images showing the front, back, label and key detail may be more useful than many repeated angles. Treat the QC count on a spreadsheet card as a research signal: it tells you warehouse imagery is available, not that the item has been approved by anyone.</p>
    <p>If a required angle is missing, check the agent’s current support options and fees before requesting anything. Available services can change, so the live account interface is the source of truth.</p>
    <h2>Decide before the parcel is packed</h2>
    <p>After reviewing the photos, record one of three outcomes: looks consistent with the order, needs a specific question, or does not match the selected option. Resolve any question through the current agent workflow before submitting the parcel for shipment. International shipping options, costs and restrictions are separate decisions and should be checked in the live checkout.</p>
  </article>

  <section class="qc-faq">
    <p class="eyebrow">E1 · QC photo FAQ</p><h2>Clear answers before you ship.</h2>
    <details open><summary>Do QC photos prove an item is authentic or high quality?</summary><p>No. Photos show a particular item at a particular moment. They can help you spot visible differences, but they do not independently verify authenticity, materials, durability or seller claims.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why does the QC image look different from the listing?</summary><p>Lighting, camera processing, screen settings and the selected variant can all change how an item appears. Check the option and overall construction first; ask a specific question if a material difference matters.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Should I rely on a spreadsheet QC badge alone?</summary><p>No. Use it to find cards with available reference images, then open the live details and make your own comparison.</p></details>
  </section>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />
</BaseLayout>
